{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q135404109","formula":"C₁₃H₂₁NO₅","hill":"C13H21NO5","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Pentamethoxyphenethylamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Pentamethoxyphenethylamine (PeMPEA), also known as 2,3,4,5,6-pentamethoxyphenethylamine (2,3,4,5,6-PeMPEA) or as 2,6-dimethoxymescaline, is a drug of the phenethylamine family related to the psychedelic drug mescaline (3,4,5-trimethoxyphenethylamine). It has been found to produce behavioral effects in animals, with about 8-fold higher potency than mescaline in the conditioned avoidance response test. The pharmacokinetics of the drug in rodents have been studied."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":618053,"mass":271.31,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C(=C(C(=C1OC)OC)OC)OC)CCN","inchikey":"SRUXXIUKHPJJRC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2,3,4,5,6-pentamethoxyphenyl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"618053","atoms":40,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.141,"y":2.407,"z":0.095,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.165,"y":-2.347,"z":0.626,"el":"O"},{"x":1.565,"y":-2.398,"z":0.261,"el":"O"},{"x":1.588,"y":2.35,"z":-0.27,"el":"O"},{"x":2.942,"y":-0.052,"z":-0.188,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.869,"y":-0.07,"z":-0.52,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.173,"y":0.031,"z":0.365,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.655,"y":0.06,"z":0.563,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.476,"y":1.217,"z":0.138,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.488,"y":-1.183,"z":0.406,"el":"C"},{"x":0.894,"y":-1.211,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":0.906,"y":1.19,"z":-0.048,"el":"C"},{"x":1.591,"y":-0.025,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.447,"y":-0.082,"z":-0.738,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.761,"y":3.395,"z":1.05,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.088,"y":-3.342,"z":-0.391,"el":"C"},{"x":2.281,"y":-2.776,"z":-0.913,"el":"C"},{"x":1.74,"y":2.761,"z":-1.627,"el":"C"},{"x":3.755,"y":0.075,"z":0.977,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.944,"